title: Defence Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: military_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD" and military_policy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/LeberJulius.jpg

= Defence Policy

We run the defence ministry. The Bundeswehr is short of soldiers, its procurement office is slow, and the military counterintelligence keeps finding right-wing extremists in the ranks. Our allies want more, and our members want less. What should we do?

- @increase_funding: Increase the defence budget.
- @decrease_funding: Cut the defence budget so that we have more for social spending.
- @reform: Reform the Bundeswehr: faster procurement, democratic leadership, and no tolerance for extremists in the ranks.
- @root: No change to defence policy.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@increase_funding
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; bundeswehr_loyalty += 0.05 if bundeswehr_loyalty < 1; bundeswehr_strength += 10; left_dissent += 5; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 3; east_relation += 1; nationalism += 1; economic_growth += 0.1

The Bundeswehr, our allies and the centre-right parties are pleased. Our members, many of whom grew up in the peace movement, are less enthusiastic.

@decrease_funding
subtitle: +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: bundeswehr_strength > 0
on-arrival: budget += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition == 1; fdp_relation -= 6; cdu_relation -= 4; bundeswehr_strength -= 10; bundeswehr_loyalty -= 0.03 if bundeswehr_loyalty > 0; east_relation -= 2; west_relation -= 1; pacifism += 1; reichswehr_goal_completed = 1; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 3; economic_growth -= 0.1

We stretch the procurement plans over more years and put the money into the budget. Warsaw, Vilnius and Washington ask whether Germany is still a reliable ally, and the Union calls it a security risk.

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1 and bundeswehr_loyalty < 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the budget. ?][? if bundeswehr_loyalty >= 1 : The Bundeswehr is already firmly rooted in democracy. ?]
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition == 1; bundeswehr_loyalty += 0.1; budget -= 1; bundeswehr_strength += 3; democratization += 1; afd_relation -= 3

We speed up procurement, strengthen the parliamentary commissioner for the armed forces, and dismiss soldiers with links to extremist groups. The AfD accuses us of purging patriots, but most soldiers welcome the clarity.
